[1m[38;5;231mDoes v1's task schema need anything beyond the baseline?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Baseline only (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mid, title, done, dueDate, createdAt, updatedAt, ownerId. Enough for due-soon and overdue reminders and nothing more. [39m
  [38;5;246mSelect this alone to skip the rest.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Priority
  [38;5;246mA low/medium/high field. Cheap to add, and gives reminder rules something to escalate on later (e.g. only nag for [39m
  [38;5;246mhigh-priority overdue tasks).[39m
[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] [38;5;153mNotes / description[39m
  [38;5;246mA free-text body per task. Purely a UI and storage concern; no effect on reminder rules.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Lists or tags
  [38;5;246mGrouping tasks into projects or tags. The most structural of these: adds a second entity or an array field, plus [39m
  [38;5;246mfiltering UI. Retrofitting means a data migration.[39m
